id chombit
name Chombit
appeared 2025
creators Pete Gonzalez
tags assembly
website https://www.hybrix.dev
description The assembly language for Chombit, the 32-bit CPU of the Hybrix virtual computer. Its 25 instructions each have a documented machine code and cycle cost, and its "framed registers" map a function's stack frame directly onto CPU registers. Devices are controlled exclusively via memory-mapped I/O. The Hybrix kernel and garbage collector are written in hand-coded Chombit assembly.
fileExtensions casm
writtenIn typescript

isOpenSource false
docs https://www.hybrix.dev/docs/assembler
country United States
funFact https://www.hybrix.dev/docs/assembler/cpu/framed_registers
 Framed registers map a function's stack frame onto CPU registers: negative indexes are parameters and positive indexes are locals, so in i:-12 and i:0 the sign tells you which is which.

example
 # -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 # fibonacci(n: int): int    (assembles to 46 bytes)
 @main.fibonacci:
     push fp
     move fp, sp
     add sp, 12
 
     # i:-16 return value
     # i:-12 arg_n
     # i:-8  return ip
     # i:-4  fp
     # i:0   a
     # i:4   b
     # i:8   next
 
     compare i:-12, 0
     if less
     fail 20 # 20 = function was called with an invalid argument
 
     move i:0, 0               # a = fibonacci(0)
     move i:4, 1               # b = fibonacci(1)
 
 @main.fibonacci.l_0:
     compare i:-12, 0
     if zero
     jump @main.fibonacci.l_1
 
     move i:8, i:0
     add i:8, i:4              # next = a + b
     move i:0, i:4             # a = b
     move i:4, i:8             # b = next
 
     add i:-12, -1
     jump @main.fibonacci.l_0
 
 @main.fibonacci.l_1:
     move i:-16, i:0
 
     add sp, -12
     pop fp
     pop ip
     fill 4

lineCommentToken #

